WEBVTT

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.860
Princess!

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.560
Good morning.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.740
Yuu-kun, mor—

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.120
Princess?

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:28.090
I-I feel like I had a weird dream.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.550
I had a nice dream.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.890
<i>Everyone was crying</i>

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.350
<i>Like a star burning blue</i>

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:45.730
<i>Where will we go? What will we see?</i>

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:50.530
<i>We're all going to change, though.</i>

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.950
<i>I don't need it, don't want it.</i>

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.060
<i>I've already given up on it</i>

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.720
<i>After so many sad farewells</i>

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.100
<i>And "take cares"</i>

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:19.420
<i>I want to like the present more than the past, 
the future more than the present.</i>

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:23.510
<i>Gradually my values have changed</i>

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:26.980
<i>I felt more grown up the more they wore away</i>

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:32.870
<i>Lies and betrayals 
are practically civilities</i>

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:36.370
<i>Everyone ages</i>

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:39.850
<i>But what about the star burning blue?</i>

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:43.190
<i>Our likes and dislikes</i>

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:46.790
<i>They'll all change at some point</i>

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.660
<i>A worn-out savior</i>

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.340
<i>A medal in a dirty ditch</i>

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.170
<i>I don't want to overlook 
their faint glimmers of light</i>

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:58.970
<i>I hear the sound still ringing from them</i>

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:04.490
<i>Let's move on a bit</i>

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.900
<b>Episode 4: Asahina Hisame and Shinonome Hangetsu</b>

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.450
Ah, Shinonome-san!

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:11.400
Hmm?

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:15.610
Hey. Morning, you two.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.780
Time for a rematch!

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.070
Training?

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.250
Sure.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:25.880
So fast!

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:42.970
Over here?!

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.090
Ludo, you said Neu hasn't changed, right?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.510
When was the last time 
you saw Neu, and where?

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.500
Not sure.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.870
You should ask Neu.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.210
Embarrassingly enough, I can't remember.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:13.500
Your eyes don't look like those of someone 
serving our Princess to protect the Earth.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.960
What are you plotting?

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:20.610
That question is just based on your 
subjective, biased assumption, isn't it?

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:21.290
Hmph.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:25.620
Your sinister gaze says more than 
enough about your evil nature.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.630
Damn mutt!

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.180
Ow! You bastard!

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:38.760
There!

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.290
By the way, do you read manga?

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.210
Yeah, I read some.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.520
Then lend me something!

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.170
I've taken a liking to shojo manga lately.

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.380
Shojo manga?

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.800
I'll train you tomorrow, too, so please!

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.050
Hmm?

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.160
Huh?

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:10.930
My stick!

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.150
Took you too long to notice.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.500
Good boy! Good boy! Well done, Saw!

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:33.190
S-Stop it! Don't call me Saw!

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.880
Just a dog in the end, huh?

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.990
Any manga you recommend?

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:41.000
<i>Magical Girl Magical Marie</i>.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.940
Oh! Did you watch yesterday's episode?

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:44.130
I did, I did!

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.970
It was so great!

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.930
Oh, Onee-chan, you're leaving already?

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.510
Welcome home, Sami.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.390
Who's that?

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:03.350
Oh, this is—

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.700
Pleasure to meet you. I'm in love!

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.660
<b>Love</b>

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.700
Inlove-san? Nice to meet you.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:14.870
<b>Inlove-san</b>

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.660
I'm Asahina Hisame.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:22.000
Well, Sami, breakfast is ready, 
so clean up when you're done.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:31.170
Hisame-san, huh?

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.470
She's a goddess.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.770
Oh, there's no breakfast here 
for you, Shinonome-san.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.300
Don't mind me!

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.980
My heart is full right now!

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:44.900
By the way,

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.950
you call yourself a hero of justice, 
but what, exactly, is your job?

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.240
My job, huh?

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.120
Once I got involved in this battle,

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:55.130
I thought, "I get to be 
a superhero protecting the Earth!"

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.480
and made those business cards right away.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.110
I thought you might be a detective 
or a lawyer or something.

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:02.380
Well...

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:04.290
A hero of justice?

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:05.980
A detective?

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.520
I get it, Shinonome-dono.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:11.770
Everyone admires heroes of justice.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:14.060
Oh, you can talk, Lizard-kun.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:17.580
Hmph. Being a warrior is cooler.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.520
Okay, I'll return them 
when I'm done reading.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.110
I finished the laundry.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.340
Good job.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:28.640
Princess.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:29.450
Yeah?

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:34.420
We should probably keep our 
objective under wraps from them.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.370
Doesn't really matter.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.690
Earth will be destroyed either way.

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:43.600
Who's on our side or not 
is a trivial matter.

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:47.180
Of course, it won't be done 
by the Biscuit Hammer.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.050
It'll be done by my fist.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.290
My apologies.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:58.870
Besides, I've already got you 
on my side, and that's enough.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.690
She's an angel.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:08.150
An angel.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:34.240
Hell, it's actually stopping?!

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:36.560
Guess I can't get a car to hit it for me.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:54.800
What do I do?

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:58.940
I can already tell continuing 
to dodge it is a losing battle.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.000
Superhero, Masked Hangetsu has arrived!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.150
S-Shinonome-san!

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:10.530
What's that lead-in for?!

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:12.720
You're not even wearing a mask.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.180
I always admired these situations!

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.750
Oh!

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:24.410
Man, you're hard!

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:29.610
Holding Field, Halberd!

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.240
I-It carved into the golem?!

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.460
A single blow's not enough?

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.950
Are its eyes not its weak point?

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:42.580
Whatever.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.760
Won't matter if I shave it all away.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:46.880
Halberd!

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.700
I-Incredible.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:55.280
The Dog Knight's Holding Field is 
the strongest among the Beast Knights,

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:57.680
save for the three Mythic Beast Knights.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:01.520
<i>Martial arts that negate both 
monstrous strength and lightning speed,</i>

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.470
<i>combined with a Holding Field spear 
that can pierce golems...</i>

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.780
<i>With those he could stop 
our Princess's ambition.</i>

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:14.160
I won, I won! Yay!

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:17.190
<i>Shinonome Hangetsu...</i>

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.900
<i>You're dangerous.</i>

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:23.790
<i>Shit! He noticed my hostility!</i>

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:28.000
Nice. That look, that bloodlust...

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:30.850
You have more potential than the Princess.

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:33.980
I'll train you anytime you like.

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:37.260
Later.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.540
Let's end it here for today.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:08.830
D-Damn it!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.450
Oh, by the way...

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:15.890
Does Hisame-san, um...

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:18.880
h-have a boyfriend?

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:21.600
My sister?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.590
What's her age?! Her job?! Her hobbies?!

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:25.900
Her favorite foods?! H-Her measurements?!

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.560
The color of her underwear?!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.390
And, uh, uh...

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:46.120
Jot Jot Jot

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:31.510
She's 27.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:34.010
She's a professor at the local university.

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:35.610
I forget what her hobbies are.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.230
She loves sweet foods, 
and I don't know her measurements.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:40.790
I'm not telling you about her underwear.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:42.200
Mhmm, mhmm...

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.740
Hey now,

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:46.120
you left out the important part 
about a boyfriend.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:47.870
Hmm...

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.460
I don't know if I should be sharing that.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.170
Whoa!

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.920
I just dropped a meal ticket 
for the French restaurant

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.130
that opened in front 
of the station last week!

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:07.570
Apparently, she doesn't have one.

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:08.480
Mhmm.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.940
<i>She sold out her own sister.</i>

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.630
Yay! A French restaurant!

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:14.900
Later.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:19.690
Oh, Amamiya-kun!

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:20.360
Yes?

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:23.360
I said I'd train you anytime,

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:24.820
but you should take it up sooner than later.

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:27.160
It's your life on the line.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.310
I'll consider it.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:36.540
Oh.

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:40.300
Hey, Amami—

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:43.210
Hey, Amamiya-kun!

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:44.800
Oh, is that Asahina-sensei?

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.010
What a coincidence. 
Nice meeting you the other day.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:49.980
Uh, Inlove-san, right?

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:52.220
<b>Inlove-san</b>

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.980
My name is Shinonome Hangetsu.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.940
<b>Shinonome Hangetsu
Private Eye, Bodyguard, Cleaning, Transportation
Handyman</b>

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.160
By the way, I'm 28 and single!

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.820
I was assisting with 
cleaning the school today.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.710
And what an honor it is!

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:06.490
Being able to get to know a beauty like you!

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:11.140
N-No, I'm just a plain woman 
obsessed with research.

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:12.340
Heavens, no!

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:15.040
Your intelligent gaze, 
your elegant black hair...

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.960
Every part of you is brimming with charm!

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:20.370
<i>He sounds like a scam artist.</i>

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:22.920
Oh, if you don't mind, have this.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.600
I was planning to eat it, 
but time got away from me.

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:31.140
This is the limited-time 
cheesecake from La Shimom!

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:32.530
Are you sure?!

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:35.100
Go ahead, go ahead. I'll see you later!

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:40.310
Shinonome-san's such a nice guy!

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:43.000
<i>This woman seems like she'd fall for scams.</i>

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:46.520
You should become a bright, 
cheerful adult like him!

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:47.530
Sure...

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:49.820
Shinonome, huh?

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:55.210
Amamiya, have you heard 
about him having a little brother?

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.020
No?

00:12:56.020 --> 00:13:00.260
There's a student one grade below you, 
called Shinonome Mikazuki.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:02.810
Mikazuki and Hangetsu...

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:05.010
They do sound related from their names.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.910
I haven't seen him for about six months.

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:12.160
I'm his advisor, so I feel bad 
just leaving him be.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.730
Could you ask Hangetsu about him some time?

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:16.560
All right.

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:20.120
Yeah, he's my little brother.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:21.470
I figured.

00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:24.470
Apparently, he hasn't been 
to school in a while,

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.400
but do you know what he's up to?

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:31.510
I remember him saying he was going to 
Southeast Asia, but what about it?

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:33.620
Why did you want to know about him?

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:36.080
Asahina-sensei wanted to know about—

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.420
Huh? Huh?

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:42.050
<b>DASH</b>

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:45.290
Guess he's going to talk to her directly.

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:48.360
Oh, I figured it out.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:49.550
Figured what out?

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:52.510
How to take care of Shinonome Hangetsu.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:57.520
I can kill him if I take 
Asahina Hisame hostage.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:00.710
Cut that out!

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:02.900
Talking of murdering for your convenience!

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:07.110
You'd be no different than 
the criminal who killed your father!

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:11.270
I know I told you.

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:15.500
I'm willing to do anything to help 
our Princess destroy this planet.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.960
Have you gone mad with power, brat?!

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:18.840
What?

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.780
Have you grown conceited after 
obtaining a Holding Field,

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:27.150
and facing death in this 
battle for the planet?

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:30.930
Don't get the wrong idea. You're not special.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.250
You're just a brat,

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:35.390
overwhelmed by fate, 
and at the mercy of this world!

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:37.720
You're dependent on others,

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:40.890
and long for naught but destruction!

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:45.640
You're like a child throwing a 
tantrum and breaking his toys

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:47.900
when things won't go the way he wants!

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.450
What's the matter? Can't argue back?

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:55.620
No, I've got nothing to say to you.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:56.410
What?

00:14:56.820 --> 00:15:00.040
I'm more than well aware of that already.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:02.380
Your lecture won't do any good.

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:06.040
Yuuhi...

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:15.850
Huh?

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:20.310
Did I forget to lock it?

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:22.790
Did I leave the lights on, too?

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:31.110
Oh, welcome back. You're late.

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:33.070
What are you doing in my home?

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:34.870
For one thing, 
how did you know where I live?

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:36.280
And what about the lock?

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:40.580
Quit sweating the small stuff.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.080
It's not small stuff!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.050
Hey! Quit wandering around!

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:46.040
Don't sniff around, you mutt!

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:48.510
You sure you want to be that pushy?

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:49.590
Huh?

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.460
I'll start marking.

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:54.680
W-Would you please stop?

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:02.420
Now! Let's watch something nice together!

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:03.480
Huh?

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:08.820
<i>Magical Burning Dragon!</i>

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.770
<i>Dragon!</i>

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:14.140
Killer moves have to be shouted out loud!

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:15.750
What's going on here?

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:15.750
<i>Dragon!</i>

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.940
It's <i>Magical Girl Magical Marie</i>.

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:17.940
<i>Dragon!</i>

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:20.200
The great anime 
Samidare-chan's watching, too.

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:20.180
<i>Dragon!</i>

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:23.070
<i>Ow! Ow! Stop! Stop!</i>

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:21.340
Uh-huh...

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:23.740
Now you've got more to talk about 
with the girl you're into!

00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:24.430
<i>Dragon!</i>

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:25.180
Good luck, man!

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:26.460
<i>Burning Dragon!</i>

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:26.460
Thanks.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:27.680
That's right!

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:28.200
<i>Dragon!</i>

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:30.920
Amamiya-kun, have you 
named your Holding Field?

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:33.130
No, not particularly.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.560
Superpowers are totally killer moves!

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:37.720
You can't get into it if you don't name it!

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:38.600
Ow. Ow.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.220
Right?! Right?!

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.430
A name, huh?

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:41.720
<i>This is the end!</i>

00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:45.980
<i>Magical Skull Crack!</i>

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.450
That looks painful.

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:50.280
<i>Crack! Crack!</i>

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:53.380
<i>Ahh! My bones! My bones!</i>

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:54.070
Did it hurt when I hit you with my tail?

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.270
It did.

00:16:57.380 --> 00:17:00.240
Did it hurt when I swatted you away?

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:01.990
It did.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:09.710
I see.

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:11.610
Yeah.

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:20.180
Sorry. Thanks for the meal.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:24.390
Seeing you enjoy it so much 
makes it all the more worth making.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:26.850
So good, so good!

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:35.240
Hmm?

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:41.280
Huh?

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:44.550
Hey! You been doing okay?

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:45.580
Dad?!

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:50.500
Oh, Dad!

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:53.060
Hey! Sami, I'm home!

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:55.050
Hm? Who are they?

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.220
Uh...

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:58.220
Right! Jogging buddies!

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:00.740
Thank you for being friends 
with my daughter.

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:03.530
N-Nice to meet you! I'm Shinonome!

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:04.680
Amamiya.

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.080
Hey, Dad, get your luggage 
out of the entryway.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:10.520
Sorry, sorry.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.460
Sami, I have a souvenir for you later.

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:14.110
Cool!

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:32.810
I wonder what the Princess's 
father does for a living.

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:36.430
Apparently, he's an author, 
but I don't know his pen name.

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:38.590
Hey! Amamiya-kun!

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:41.550
Are you free tonight?

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.510
Huh? Well...

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:46.510
Sorry! I was asking Asahina-sensei out

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:50.880
and said, "Don't you want to 
see Amamiya-kun when he's drunk?"

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:53.230
Please! Play along with us!

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:56.820
I don't mind doing it, 
but I've never had liquor before.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:59.780
What?! When you're already twenty?!

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:02.340
You're a real weirdo!

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:04.650
I don't want to hear that from you.

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.200
<b>Nonbe</b>

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.200
<b>Non</b>

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:18.380
That's not bad.

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:19.530
Oh!

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.510
Look at you drink, cheeky boy.

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.720
All right, let's pound them down!

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:26.680
Well, it's your first time, so not too much.

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:33.940
Excuse me! Two orders of warm sake!

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.550
And a mug of plum sour!

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:37.390
And a sweet potato shochu on the rocks.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:41.610
That reminds me, you've been 
to France, haven't you, Hisame-san?

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:42.530
Yeah.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.710
Sami used to be real sick,

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:48.620
and my mother, a doctor, 
went there to research her illness,

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.580
so she brought me with her at the time.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:54.150
And Sami-chan stayed 
behind in Japan with Dad?

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:56.040
Mother

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:56.040
<b>Father</b>

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:55.250
That's right.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:20:00.760
About three years ago, I heard 
Sami suddenly got better,

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:04.170
so I came back by myself to see how she was.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.740
Then our damn dad...

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:13.900
He told me to look after Sami and 
disappeared the moment I returned!

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:16.360
I-I see.

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:19.770
He's always traveling around 
and writing his novels!

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:22.370
He only ever comes home a few times a year!

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:24.460
Excuse me! Another sweet 
potato on the rocks!

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:27.040
So Dad's an author?

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:29.540
<i>Quit calling me "Dad"...</i>

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.450
Apparently, his books sell well.

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:34.960
Though I've never read one.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.220
You haven't?!

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:40.700
Mom and Sami say it's nice 
that he's a free spirit,

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:42.510
but he's just being irresponsible!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:43.970
<b>BAM!</b>

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:46.540
Poor man.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:51.090
So, yeah. That's why I was 
feeling a need to drink today.

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:55.270
Can you keep up, Shinonome-san?

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:58.520
Yeah! I'll follow you 
into the depths of hell!

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:01.380
Excuse me! One more please!

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:03.480
He switched to sake at some point, too.

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:05.120
He drinks like a fish.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:13.450
<b>Nonbe</b>

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:13.450
<b>Non</b>

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:13.450
<b>Nonbe</b>

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:09.100
That's the spirit, Amamiya! Drink more!

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.770
Keep the sake coming!

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:17.590
Can you stand?

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:19.380
N-No way.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:21.130
<i>I can't carry both of them.</i>

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:22.840
<i>I'll have to call the Princess.</i>

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:28.620
Sami, where's Dad?

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.760
He went out somewhere after eating dinner.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:36.600
That man just can't stay put, can he?

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:40.090
Do you hate Dad?

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:42.220
I don't hate him,

00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:43.570
but I can't respect him.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:49.590
Wandering around at his age, 
doing whatever he pleases...

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:52.490
How can he call himself an adult?

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:56.510
I think adults are big kids, 
like Shinonome-san and Dad,

00:21:56.510 --> 00:21:59.290
who seem to be enjoying life.

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:02.020
Thanks.

00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:03.360
Are you okay?

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:04.670
Yeah.

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:07.880
Let me tell you what I think about adults!

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:12.460
We adults smile to show 
how fun being an adult is

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:14.810
and make kids jealous of us!

00:22:15.170 --> 00:22:19.030
Because one of our jobs is to teach 
them that life is filled with hope!

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:22.230
<i>Now that he mentions it,</i>

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:24.880
<i>my Dad was smiling all the time, too.</i>

00:22:24.880 --> 00:22:26.470
<i>So did Grandpa back then.</i>

00:22:32.010 --> 00:22:34.250
Adults, huh?

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:40.370
I wonder what kind of adults you 
and Sami will turn out to be.

00:22:57.060 --> 00:23:05.230
<i>Looking back to those times, 
I always thought</i>

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:09.820
<i>It was hard to live life true to myself.</i>

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:13.490
<i>I recall those times.</i>

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:17.040
<i>I wanted to forget, 
but now it's different.</i>

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:22.790
<i>Back then we stared at that same sky.</i>

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:29.420
<i>I'll never forget you, 
or our endless dreams</i>

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:35.930
<i>As we gazed at that sky 
after fate brought us together</i>

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:41.560
<i>I dream of us together, 
of those days I remember</i>

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:43.730
<i>But dreams end and I wake up</i>

00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:48.280
<i>Seeking the future</i>

00:23:49.150 --> 00:23:54.370
<i>I reach for the light,</i>

00:23:55.200 --> 00:24:00.750
<i>Always thinking of you in</i>

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:13.720
<i>every little thing</i>

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:26.900
<b>Next Episode:
The Knight, Shinonome Hangetsu</b>
